On 4/11/09, tijlan <pascal.akihiko@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> So, I guess "lo broda to be da bei de toi cu brode" is grammatical
> too?

Yes, because "be da bei de" is a valid fragment. You can't guarantee
that the linked arguments will correspond syntactically to "broda"
there, although semantically that is of course the obvious
interpretation.

> And is this "toi" elidable: "lo broda to be da bei de cu brode"?

Yes. Personally, I never elide the three types of terminators that
follow a "text", namely TOI, LIhU and TUhU, becuse I find the result
confusing. I would even suggest changing the grammar so that those
three are made not elidable, but that probably won't happen.

